le="left:18.1%;top:92.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-documents-and-your-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents and your account</h2><p class="gd-p">The menu has four links: <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: your agreements, receipts, statements and uploads. Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Download</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>: your contact details (<b class="gd-ui">Save</b>), sign-in, drivers and your Card on File.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>: notices from us. Use <b class="gd-ui">Mark as read</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as read</b>, and choose which optional emails you get. A number on <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> in the menu is how many notices you have not read.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/documents</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/renter-15-documents-desktop-fd428a63.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.8%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Your legal name is locked once you are verified. To change it, call or message us. To change your email, open Profile, Sign-in and press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b>: we send a link to the new address and tell the old one, and the email changes when the link is opened.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-sign-in-with-your-phone-number" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign in with your phone number</h2><p class="gd-p">No password needed: we text you a 6-digit code from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/sign-in</span>, press <b class="gd-ui">Use my phone number instead</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter your mobile number and press <b class="gd-ui">Text me a code</b>. Codes go to Canadian mobile numbers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type the 6-digit code from the text (on most phones it fills itself in), or press <b class="gd-ui">Sign in</b>. The code works for 5 minutes; <b class="gd-ui">Send a new code</b> after a minute if it did not arrive.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To sign in by phone every time, open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>, enter the code we text you, then choose <b class="gd-ui">My phone number (a code by text)</b> under Sign in with. The sign-in page then opens on your phone number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>New here? On Create account, press Sign up with my phone number instead: your name, your mobile number and the code. An account made by phone has no email yet: you can send requests, accept offers and sign, and the pay page asks for your email before your first payment, for the receipts. A booking request you sent earlier with the same mobile number is added to your account once the code is checked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-texts-or-email-how-we-reach-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email: how we reach you</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose Email, Text or Both. Texts are short, come from the CarmaCars number and link to the page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>. It is saved at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Texts go to the phone you verified with a code (Sign-in, above). Until you verify one, we email you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Signed agreements, statements and receipts are always emailed when we have your email. On Text you also get a text with a link to view or download them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No texts from 9 pm to 8 am, except urgent ones such as a late return. Reply STOP to any text to stop texts (we confirm with one text); text START to turn them back on.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>You can also choose in the booking request (How should we reach you?) and when you sign up with your phone number, where Text is chosen for you.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> in your account.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every rental earns 1 point per dollar of the rental charge when it closes. 100 points are worth $1 off the rental charge of a later booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">More ways to earn are listed on the page: refer a friend with your link (you both get points at their first rental), follow us, review your rental on carmacars.ca, review us on Google (press <b class="gd-ui">I posted my review</b> and give the name on it), a damage-free rental, your birthday and your first rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Get my code</b> turns points into a code of your own, from 500 points. Type it in the promo code box of your request. An unused code can be given back for the points.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your tier comes from the points you earned in the last 12 months (using points never lowers it): <b class="gd-ui">Gold</b> from 1,000 points gives Instant Book (your request is booked at once), <b class="gd-ui">Platinum</b> from 15,000 gives <b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b> (request a car even on dates it shows as taken; we answer within 4 hours), <b class="gd-ui">Black</b> from 60,000 gives one free rental day a year as a code. Each tier keeps the perks below it. The bar shows how many points to the next tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your discounts</b> lists every code you hold (from points, your tier, referrals, our team, the free day): what it gives, when it ends, and whether it is unused, on a request or used, with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>. When you send a request, tap the code under <b class="gd-ui">Use a saved discount</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Points end 12 months after your last rental or redemption. We email you a month before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-your-trip-in-your-calendar-or-wallet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your trip in your calendar or wallet</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed booking, <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b> adds the pickup and the return. The confirmation email has the same link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> shows when it is available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer when your offer is ready, before pickup and return, for payments and when we message you, even with CarmaCars closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications when your browser asks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>, untick anything you do not want. Your choice applies to all your devices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> to see one. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off on this device</b> stops them there; <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes another device off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first: in Safari tap <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>. Open CarmaCars from your Home Screen, sign in and turn alerts on in Profile (iOS 16.4 or later).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Alerts come as well as your emails and texts, never instead of them. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am. Sign-in links and codes never come as alerts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-delete-my-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Delete my account</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> and scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>, add a reason if you like, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We settle anything still open (a rental, a deposit), delete your account and email you within 30 days. Changed your mind before then? Press <b class="gd-ui">Keep my account</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>We keep rental agreements, receipts and tax records as the law requires. Everything else, including your licence and selfie photos, is deleted.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-odometer-and-fuel-at-pickup-and-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at pickup and return</h2><p class="gd-p">When you check the car in or out yourself:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Add a photo of the dashboard (the odometer and the fuel gauge). It can come from your camera roll. We read it and ask, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel level.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Take a selfie in front of the car with your camera.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Your return: km and fuel</b> on your booking shows the km driven, the km included and any km over, the fuel compared with pickup, and the charge for each. The photo report shows both dashboard photos.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-earn-reward-points" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Earn reward points</h2><p class="gd-p">Review your rental (add a photo for extra points), review us on Google, follow us from your Rewards page, refer a friend, and every rental after your first earns points too. See them all on <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-rewards-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rewards and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Earn points for a photo with your review and for every rental after your first; every way to earn is on your Rewards page.</li><li>A fuel shortfall at the return is priced from the car&#39;s tank and the local pump price, plus a refuelling fee, and checked by our team before any charge.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-thank-the-team" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Thank the team</h2><p class="gd-p">Happy with the service? On your booking after the return, or from the link in the &quot;Returned&quot; email, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a tip for the team</b>: 10, 15 or 20% or any amount, by card. It goes to the people who looked after your rental.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, charges and fees, receipts, booking confirmations and changes, pickup and return reminders, and safety messages.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'chapter', 'apply-and-get-your-car-listed', 'Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.

## Home at a glance

1. The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.
2. At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month''s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.
3. Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or **Payouts** for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.
4. Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press **Add a vehicle**.

![](/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1270; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 19.1 8.1, 2 72.9 30.7, 3 31.2 85.0")

> Tip: When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.

## A car''s page

Open Cars, then a car.

1. The top shows the car''s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.
2. Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.
3. This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. **Book it for myself** reserves it for you.
4. Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.

![](/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1242; address: carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7; pins: 1 55.6 25.1, 2 83.3 38.0, 3 36.5 54.5, 4 81.2 67.0")

While a car is being set up, its page also shows the **Onboarding** checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission and the insurance.

## Where your car is

Once your car has its tracker, its page shows **Where your car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported, and **Open on the map**. Below it, the trips of the last 30 days: when, how far, and where each started and ended.

1. Open **Cars** and the car.
2. No tracker on the car yet? It says **No tracker yet**.
3. You see the location and the trips only. The renter''s name and the booking stay private, as before.

## Tracker alerts

Once your car has its tracker, its page shows **Tracker alerts** below **Where your car is**: what the tracker recorded in the last 30 days.

- Speeding, harsh driving, the car outside Ontario, driving after the return time, the tracker unplugged or tampered with, or the car parked at an impound lot.
- Leaving Ontario or leaving Canada: we tell you at once, and CarmaCars calls the renter.
- Each alert says what happened and when, with **See the place**.
- We also tell you by email, text or the app when one happens.

1. Open **Cars** and the car.
2. Nothing there? It says nothing was recorded.
3. To stop these alerts or change how they reach you, open **Notifications** and turn **Tracker alert on your car** off or on.

> Note: There is nothing for you to do. CarmaCars handles each one with the renter and collects any charge with its evidence. You see the event and the place only, never the renter or the booking.

## The onboarding checklist

Home and each car''s page show the same **Onboarding checklist**. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example "First: terms approved"), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as **Check and sign** or **Upload the ownership permit**.

## Change an onboarding photo

A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter? Open the car, then **Your onboarding photos**.

1. Press **Replace** and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.
2. Or press **Remove**, then **Remove the photo**.

> Good to know: Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.

## Add several cars at once

Open **Cars**, then **Add cars from a VIN list**.

1. Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.
2. Press **Preview**: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.
3. Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press **Add**.

Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Price limits

Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.

1. **Cars**, **Price limits for every car**, at the bottom: type a **Minimum a day** and a **Maximum a day** in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press **Save price limits**.
2. One car different? Open it: **Price limits** has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.
3. Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.

## Studio photos (release 48)

- We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.
- Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.
- We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in **Account**, **Notifications**.', 'Home and your vehicles', 'What Home shows, each car''s page, adding a car and new listing photos.',
