> Good to know: Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.

## Add several cars at once

Open **Cars**, then **Add cars from a VIN list**.

1. Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.
2. Press **Preview**: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.
3. Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press **Add**.

Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Price limits

Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.

1. **Cars**, **Price limits for every car**, at the bottom: type a **Minimum a day** and a **Maximum a day** in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press **Save price limits**.
2. One car different? Open it: **Price limits** has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.
3. Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.

## Studio photos (release 48)

- We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.
- Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.
- We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in **Account**, **Notifications**.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.</p><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-home-at-a-glance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Home at a glance</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month&#39;s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or <b class="gd-ui">Payouts</b> for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a vehicle</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1270"><img src="/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1270"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.1%;top:8.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:30.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.2%;top:85%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-a-car-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Cars, then a car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows the car&#39;s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> reserves it for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1242"><img src="/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1242"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:55.6%;top:25.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:38%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.5%;top:54.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:67%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">While a car is being set up, its page also shows the <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission and the insurance.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-where-your-car-is" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where your car is</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported, and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>. Below it, the trips of the last 30 days: when, how far, and where each started and ended.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No tracker on the car yet? It says <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You see the location and the trips only. The renter&#39;s name and the booking stay private, as before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-tracker-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alerts</b> below <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: what the tracker recorded in the last 30 days.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Speeding, harsh driving, the car outside Ontario, driving after the return time, the tracker unplugged or tampered with, or the car parked at an impound lot.</li><li>Leaving Ontario or leaving Canada: we tell you at once, and CarmaCars calls the renter.</li><li>Each alert says what happened and when, with <b class="gd-ui">See the place</b>.</li><li>We also tell you by email, text or the app when one happens.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing there? It says nothing was recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To choose which alerts reach you and how, open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>: each tracker alert has its own switches (see Tracker alerts under Notices). The page lists every alert either way.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>There is nothing for you to do. CarmaCars handles each one with the renter and collects any charge with its evidence. You see the event and the place only, never the renter or the booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-the-onboarding-checklist" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The onboarding checklist</h2><p class="gd-p">Home and each car&#39;s page show the same <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example &quot;First: terms approved&quot;), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Upload the ownership permit</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-change-an-onboarding-photo" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an onboarding photo</h2><p class="gd-p">A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter? Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Your onboarding photos</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove the photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-add-several-cars-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add several cars at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a VIN list</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-price-limits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Price limits</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Price limits for every car</b>, at the bottom: type a <b class="gd-ui">Minimum a day</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Maximum a day</b> in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One car different? Open it: <b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b> has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-pickup-and-return-records-cars-you-referred-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> shows the car&#39;s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> shows their cars&#39; bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-studio-photos-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio photos (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.</li><li>Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.</li><li>We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', 'chapter', 'bookings-and-your-own-use', 'Your fees are debited from your bank account on the 15th, after a notice. Your payout for the month before arrives on the 10th, with a statement.

## How your fees work

- Each car has two monthly fees: an insurance fee and a tracker fee. They are due every month, rented or not.
- The tracker fee starts the day the car''s tracker is installed. The tracker install fee has its own invoice.
- Before a car goes live you pay the first and last month amount we agreed with you (usually two months of the insurance fee, or the exact amount we agreed).
- Your amounts are the ones we agreed for each car, to the cent. Any other fee we agreed, for example a registration fee, comes on its own invoice with each line, its quantity and whether HST applies.
- Cars shows each car''s terms: the insurance fee and tracker fee a month and the Revenue Share, since when they apply, and any change coming. Open a car for its History: every period of terms and every notice we sent (Download the notice).
- Lower amounts apply from the date in our notice. A higher fee comes with 30 days'' written notice; a higher Revenue Share applies only if you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. A month whose fee changes part way is billed per day at each amount.
- One invoice per car. Registry, inspection and appraisal costs are not billed by us unless we agreed to pay them for you; then they are on an invoice of their own.

An invoice we cancel shows Void with the reason, and the invoice that replaces it. Nothing is debited for a void invoice. Every invoice has Download PDF.

## The monthly debit, step by step

:::flow
Notice day | 10 days before: your invoices and one email with the total
The 15th | Each invoice is debited from your account
Cleared | The invoice shows Paid and you get a receipt
Insufficient funds? | A $50.00 Late Fee once, and the same amount tried again within 30 days
:::

- A debit is never more than its notice said. Each invoice shows "will be debited on" with the date.
- If your bank returns a debit for insufficient funds, we add the $50.00 Late Fee to that invoice once and try the original amount again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of your Enrollment Agreement sets out. The Late Fee is collected with your next debit.
- Returned for another reason (for example a closed account)? We do not try again and add no Late Fee. We pause your debit and email you: pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under Account > Banking.
- Returned again after the retry? The invoice is in arrears and we contact you.
- Any debit that was missed and not paid since comes off your next monthly revenue statement: it shows there as a deduction with the invoice number.
- You can always pay an invoice by card from its page before the debit day.
- On your bank statement the debit shows our company''s legal name, operating as CarmaCars.

### What each amount is

Every debit email lists each amount in one line: the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment or late fee), the month it covers and how it was worked out. A car that joined during the month says "prorated: 20 of 30 days". A car on a flat monthly payment pays no monthly fee for those days. Each line opens its invoice.

### When we can''t collect a debit

We email you, and our staff see the same reason:

- "No bank debit set up": set it up under **Account** > **Banking**. Nothing is taken until you do.
- "Owner cancelled the debit at their bank": set it up again under **Account** > **Banking**.
- "Amount went up after the notice": we send a new notice for the new amount and debit it after the notice period.
- "The bank sent the payment back": see above. Pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under **Account** > **Banking**.

## Set up the automatic debit

Do this once. Without it, we email you on each notice day to set it up.

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Automatic debit of your fees, press **Set up pre-authorized debit**.
2. Read the agreement and press **Continue to my bank details**.
3. Enter your bank details and press **Save the bank account**. Banking then shows the account and the next debit.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-52316739.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 752; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 96.2 36.8")

## Pay an invoice now

1. Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.
2. Choose Card (paid at once) and press **Pay $...**.
3. Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press **Authorize debit of $...**.
4. Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.

![](/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 742; address: carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050; pins: 2 6.9 52.6, 3 38.2 52.6, 4 11.5 80.5")

> Tip: Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says "Paid by e-Transfer on" the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.

## Tell us where to pay you

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.
2. Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).
3. Press **Submit payout details**. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg "desktop; size: 990 642; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 50.5 25.7, 2 90.9 45.5, 3 30.3 89.7")

## Statements and payouts

1. This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.
2. Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see each booking that counts toward your revenue (a booking paid by the renter always does; an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your calendar are left out), the revenue share, deductions and the payout.
3. Press **Download PDF** to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.
4. Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.

![](/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 792; address: carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74; pins: 2 16.0 30.6, 1 66.0 40.9")

> Good to know: Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car''s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.

### Fees taken from your statement
If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement") and reads **Paid from statement**. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.

### A flat monthly payment and your agreement
If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement**: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows **Check and sign** for the new agreement.

## Repairs and partner credits

If CarmaCars turns it on for you, **Money** > **Statements** also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.

## Statement periods and price limits (release 35)

- Each statement covers the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th pays it. A rental across the cutoff is paid for the days in each period, never twice.
- Amounts a renter still owes are listed apart on your statement and paid on the statement after we collect them.
- Set the lowest and highest daily rate for every car or one car: short-notice pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers stay between them.

## Your forecast (release 48)

**Home** has a **Forecast** section: the next 12 months of each of your cars, with its projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open a car to see its months; with several cars, the line on top adds them up.

- Every car starts from the GTA''s rental season: January and February are quiet, March Break and the long weekends pick up, July and August are the busiest, and December brings holiday travel.
- Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in, and it counts for more each month: half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. Under each car you see how its forecast is made.
- Projected owner revenue uses your car''s own statements of the last 12 months, per day booked; a newer car uses its daily rate less the Revenue Share.
- Bookings hidden from you are never counted.

Each statement also has a **Forecast** line: whether next month is projected higher or lower than the statement''s month, by how many points of occupancy and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).

> Note: A forecast is an estimate, not a promise. Your statements and payouts are always what your car actually earned.', 'Fees, payments and payouts', 'How fees are billed, the monthly debit, paying an invoice, statements and payouts.',
  'Your fees are debited from your bank account on the 15th, after a notice. Your payout for the month before arrives on the 10th, with a statement.

## How your fees work

- Each car has two monthly fees: an insurance fee and a tracker fee. They are due every month, rented or not.
- The tracker fee starts the day the car''s tracker is installed. The tracker install fee has its own invoice.
- Before a car goes live you pay the first and last month amount we agreed with you (usually two months of the insurance fee, or the exact amount we agreed).
- Your amounts are the ones we agreed for each car, to the cent. Any other fee we agreed, for example a registration fee, comes on its own invoice with each line, its quantity and whether HST applies.
- Cars shows each car''s terms: the insurance fee and tracker fee a month and the Revenue Share, since when they apply, and any change coming. Open a car for its History: every period of terms and every notice we sent (Download the notice).
- Lower amounts apply from the date in our notice. A higher fee comes with 30 days'' written notice; a higher Revenue Share applies only if you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. A month whose fee changes part way is billed per day at each amount.
- One invoice per car. Registry, inspection and appraisal costs are not billed by us unless we agreed to pay them for you; then they are on an invoice of their own.

An invoice we cancel shows Void with the reason, and the invoice that replaces it. Nothing is debited for a void invoice. Every invoice has Download PDF.

## The monthly debit, step by step

:::flow
Notice day | 10 days before: your invoices and one email with the total
The 15th | Each invoice is debited from your account
Cleared | The invoice shows Paid and you get a receipt
Insufficient funds? | A Late Fee once (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST), and the same amount tried again within 30 days
:::

- A debit is never more than its notice said. Each invoice shows "will be debited on" with the date.
- If your bank returns a debit for insufficient funds, we add the Late Fee to that invoice once (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST; $50.00 on an invoice with no insurance) and try the original amount again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of your Enrollment Agreement sets out. The Late Fee is collected with your next debit.
- Returned for another reason (for example a closed account)? We do not try again and add no Late Fee. We pause your debit and email you: pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under Account > Banking.
- Returned again after the retry? The invoice is in arrears and we contact you.
- Any debit that was missed and not paid since comes off your next monthly revenue statement: it shows there as a deduction with the invoice number.
- You can always pay an invoice by card from its page before the debit day.
- On your bank statement the debit shows our company''s legal name, operating as CarmaCars.

### What each amount is

Every debit email lists each amount in one line: the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment or late fee), the month it covers and how it was worked out. A car that joined during the month says "prorated: 20 of 30 days". A car on a flat monthly payment pays no monthly fee for those days. Each line opens its invoice.

### When we can''t collect a debit

We email you, and our staff see the same reason:

- "No bank debit set up": set it up under **Account** > **Banking**. Nothing is taken until you do.
- "Owner cancelled the debit at their bank": set it up again under **Account** > **Banking**.
- "Amount went up after the notice": we send a new notice for the new amount and debit it after the notice period.
- "The bank sent the payment back": see above. Pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under **Account** > **Banking**.

## Set up the automatic debit

Do this once. Without it, we email you on each notice day to set it up.

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Automatic debit of your fees, press **Set up pre-authorized debit**.
2. Read the agreement and press **Continue to my bank details**.
3. Enter your bank details and press **Save the bank account**. Banking then shows the account and the next debit.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-52316739.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 752; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 96.2 36.8")

## Pay an invoice now

1. Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.
2. Choose Card (paid at once) and press **Pay $...**.
3. Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press **Authorize debit of $...**.
4. Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.

![](/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 742; address: carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050; pins: 2 6.9 52.6, 3 38.2 52.6, 4 11.5 80.5")

> Tip: Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says "Paid by e-Transfer on" the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.

## Tell us where to pay you

1. Open **Account** > **Banking**. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.
2. Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).
3. Press **Submit payout details**. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.

![](/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg "desktop; size: 990 642; address: carmacars.ca/owner/banking; pins: 1 50.5 25.7, 2 90.9 45.5, 3 30.3 89.7")

## Statements and payouts

1. This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.
2. Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see each booking that counts toward your revenue (a booking paid by the renter always does; an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your calendar are left out), the revenue share, deductions and the payout.
3. Press **Download PDF** to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.
4. Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.

![](/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 792; address: carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74; pins: 2 16.0 30.6, 1 66.0 40.9")

> Good to know: Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car''s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.

### Fees taken from your statement
If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement") and reads **Paid from statement**. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.

### A flat monthly payment and your agreement
If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement**: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows **Check and sign** for the new agreement.

## Repairs and partner credits

If CarmaCars turns it on for you, **Money** > **Statements** also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.

## Statement periods and price limits (release 35)

- Each statement covers the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th pays it. A rental across the cutoff is paid for the days in each period, never twice.
- Amounts a renter still owes are listed apart on your statement and paid on the statement after we collect them.
- Set the lowest and highest daily rate for every car or one car: short-notice pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers stay between them.

## Your forecast (release 48)

**Home** has a **Forecast** section: the next 12 months of each of your cars, with its projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open a car to see its months; with several cars, the line on top adds them up.

- Every car starts from the GTA''s rental season: January and February are quiet, March Break and the long weekends pick up, July and August are the busiest, and December brings holiday travel.
- Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in, and it counts for more each month: half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. Under each car you see how its forecast is made.
- Projected owner revenue uses your car''s own statements of the last 12 months, per day booked; a newer car uses its daily rate less the Revenue Share.
- Bookings hidden from you are never counted.

Each statement also has a **Forecast** line: whether next month is projected higher or lower than the statement''s month, by how many points of occupancy and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).

> Note: A forecast is an estimate, not a promise. Your statements and payouts are always what your car actually earned.

## Charges on your own bookings (release 48)

1. When you book your own car, for yourself or for someone else, you are responsible for what happens during it: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and any other fee.
2. Each charge is added only with its evidence (photos, readings, the notice or the receipt). You get an email that lists each charge and the evidence it rests on.
3. It is due at once. We charge the card you have on file. If you have no card on file, we start a pre-authorized debit from your bank account the same day.
4. If there is no payment method on file, or the charge fails, you get an invoice with a **pay** link, and reminders.
5. An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the next statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from your next statement as its own line.

## Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)

1. If your insurance is not paid on time (the debit on the 15th fails, or the invoice is unpaid after its due date), a Late Fee of 5% of the unpaid insurance is added to that invoice once, plus HST on the fee. Insurance itself has no HST.
2. You get a reminder 3 days before the due date while the invoice is unpaid, and an email when the fee is added.
3. The unpaid insurance and the Late Fee are deducted from your next statement by themselves, as two separate lines. You can pay the invoice from its page before that.
4. This replaces the $50 Late Fee for insurance. It is in section 4.4 and Schedule B of your agreement; you accept the update in the box that opens, without signing again.
