  '<p class="gd-p">Keep your details up to date, read our notices, and know how to take a car out of the program.</p><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-notifications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notifications</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Account &gt; Notifications lists our messages: trips that are complete, payments and listing news, with your email preferences beside them. We do not email you when a booking comes in or changes, because many bookings are cancelled: the bookings coming up are always under Cars &gt; Bookings. We email you when a trip is complete and the car is back (the dates, the days, the distance driven when it was recorded and your share of the trip; while your share is not shown to you yet, the email says it will show on your next statement), and once a week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as read</b> on one, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as read</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/notifications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/692"><img src="/guides/img/owner-14-notifications-desktop-8e58b95e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="692"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.1%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-your-profile" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your profile</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Update your phone and address, then press Save. To change the email you sign in with, press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b> under Sign-in: type the new address, open the link we send to it (the old address is told too), and your email changes everywhere.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your agreements shows your legal name and how you are enrolled. A change to these means new agreements, so call or message us.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/profile</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/872"><img src="/guides/img/owner-15-profile-desktop-874dd23d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="872"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.2%;top:84.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.4%;top:21.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-texts-or-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>: completed trips, payouts, invoices and documents to sign by a short text with a link. Texts need a phone you verified with a code. Statements, invoices and signed documents are always emailed too. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-take-a-car-out-of-the-program" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take a car out of the program</h2><p class="gd-p">You give 30 days&#39; notice for that car only. Your other cars stay in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Cars and the car. Read Leaving: when the notice ends and what happens to your last fees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give notice</b>. Add a Reason (optional).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give exit notice</b>. The car&#39;s page then shows its exit date.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer when one of your cars is booked, when a booking changes, for payouts and payments, incidents and documents to sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications when your browser asks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>, choose the topics. Your choice applies to all your devices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> shows one. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off on this device</b> stops them there; <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes another device off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Once your application is approved, your portal asks once whether to turn alerts on: press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not now</b> (it is not asked again until a later approval). On a phone, once the CarmaCars app is in the stores, the invitation offers <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> instead.</p><p class="gd-p">On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>), then open it from there and turn alerts on. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-delete-my-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Delete my account</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, delete my account</b>. We settle your cars, payouts and invoices first (a car under your agreement leaves the program with 30 days&#39; notice), then delete your account and email you. <b class="gd-ui">Keep my account</b> withdraws the request. Agreements, statements and tax records are kept as the law requires.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-your-name-and-password-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your name and password (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Profile. <b class="gd-ui">Save my display name</b> changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b>, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b> sends you to the password page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-your-week-every-monday-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your week, every Monday (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Monday morning (about 9:00 Toronto time) you get one email, only if there was something to tell. For each car: the trips completed last week with their dates and your share (a trip whose amount is not shown to you yet says it is on your statement), your confirmed bookings in the next 14 days (dates only), and your earnings so far this month, which are provisional until your statement. Only bookings that count toward your revenue are listed. Nothing to set up; it is on by default.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-sharing-your-location-at-a-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sharing your location at a handover</h2><p class="gd-p">With your permission, your location is shared with our team only two hours either side of a pickup or return of your car. Turn it off any time in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Location on the live map</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, invoices and fees, statements, payouts and receipts, and incidents on your car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">New bookings on your cars</b> is off to start with, because many bookings change before the trip. Turn it on if you want to hear about each one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="notices-profile-and-leaving-tracker-alerts-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker alerts (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">These start when your tracker is installed. Until then each one says so, and your choice is kept.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>, under Tracker alerts, each alert has its own switches.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On to start with: possible theft (also the car leaving Ontario or Canada), tracker disconnected or tampered with, crash or impact, and at an impound lot, auto shop or shipping port.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Off to start with: vehicle health warning, over 180 km/h (it still shows on the car&#39;s page) and the weekly driving summary (speeding, hard braking and acceleration, late-night trips, and kilometres against the allowance). Turn on the ones you want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An alert names your car and what happened. It never names the renter or the booking. CarmaCars gets the same alert and acts on it.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'people-and-access', 'chapter', 'getting-around-admin', 'Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.

## Portals and sign-in

Open **People** > **Portals and view as**. Every portal has a card.

1. Each card links to **Its sign-in page**, the address to send that person.
2. Choose a person in the list on the card.
3. Press **Open as this person** to see that portal as they see it.

> Good to know: The site''s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend''s test inboxes) are marked "Test account" in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 65.9 30.2, 2 58.1 39.4, 3 51.6 45.6")

## Invite a person

Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.

1. Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.
2. Fill in the Name and Email.
3. For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.
4. Press **Invite**. The link in the email works for 24 hours.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 360; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 18.8 40.8, 2 50.0 40.8, 3 18.8 66.7, 4 9.8 87.8")

> Tip: Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People > Owners and People > Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.

## Add an investor

1. Open **People** > **Investors** and press **Add an investor**.
2. Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).
3. Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer''s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).
4. Invite now is ticked: press **Add and invite**. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.

## Send a password link

For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.

1. Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.
2. On their row, press **Send password link**. They get "Reset your CarmaCars password", valid for 24 hours.
3. **View as (...)** on the same row opens their portal, read only.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 440; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 74.8 6.6, 2 68.2 28.6, 3 84.1 28.6")

## View as: see what someone sees

1. A red banner says "Viewing as Name (email), read only." on every page.
2. Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.
3. Press **Exit** to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.

![](/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 620; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 48.6 4.5, 3 94.4 4.5")

> Watch out: Can''t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.

## The audit log

**Settings** > **Logs**, the **Changes** tab, shows who changed what, and when.

1. Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.
2. Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.
3. Search by table, record id or value.

![](/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/audit; pins: 1 22.6 31.1, 2 39.0 46.4, 3 89.6 20.7")

## Staff and roles

**People** > **Team** opens Staff and roles.

1. Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then **Invite**.
2. Each row has **Send password link**, **View as (...)** and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).
3. Press **End access** to close their staff portal at once. **Restore** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 780; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff; pins: 1 20.8 59.0, 2 94.4 86.7, 3 83.3 92.6")

## Admin access

**Settings**, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.

1. The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site''s nightly checks sign in with.
2. Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.
3. Change the list only if the business''s Admin address changes.

## Staff scorecards

See how each assistant is doing against the targets.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Scorecard**.
2. By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 350; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 2 21.1 42.9")

## Sales by staff member

See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only **Welcome**, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person''s member tag ("Name - Position") with Copy and the steps; I joined needs **I set my member tag**. The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.

## Work chats only

All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.

## Data to check on each record (release 48)

Every portal checks the person''s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings > Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. **Send reminder** sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.

## Updated agreements to accept (release 48)

When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and **Accept and continue**. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.

Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario''s Employment Standards Act requires).

## People on the live map

The live map (Visitors, and Cars > Fleet tracking) has a **People** layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone''s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job''s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.', 'People and access', 'Portals and sign-in, invitations, password links, View as, staff and scorecards.',
  'Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.

## Portals and sign-in

Open **People** > **Portals and view as**. Every portal has a card.

1. Each card links to **Its sign-in page**, the address to send that person.
2. Choose a person in the list on the card.
3. Press **Open as this person** to see that portal as they see it.

> Good to know: The site''s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend''s test inboxes) are marked "Test account" in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 65.9 30.2, 2 58.1 39.4, 3 51.6 45.6")

## Invite a person

Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.

1. Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.
2. Fill in the Name and Email.
3. For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.
4. Press **Invite**. The link in the email works for 24 hours.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 360; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 18.8 40.8, 2 50.0 40.8, 3 18.8 66.7, 4 9.8 87.8")

> Tip: Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People > Owners and People > Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.

## Add an investor

1. Open **People** > **Investors** and press **Add an investor**.
2. Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).
3. Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer''s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).
4. Invite now is ticked: press **Add and invite**. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.

## Send a password link

For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.

1. Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.
2. On their row, press **Send password link**. They get "Reset your CarmaCars password", valid for 24 hours.
3. **View as (...)** on the same row opens their portal, read only.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 440; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 74.8 6.6, 2 68.2 28.6, 3 84.1 28.6")

## View as: see what someone sees

1. A red banner says "Viewing as Name (email), read only." on every page.
2. Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.
3. Press **Exit** to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.

![](/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 620; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 48.6 4.5, 3 94.4 4.5")

> Watch out: Can''t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.

## The audit log

**Settings** > **Logs**, the **Changes** tab, shows who changed what, and when.

1. Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.
2. Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.
3. Search by table, record id or value.

![](/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/audit; pins: 1 22.6 31.1, 2 39.0 46.4, 3 89.6 20.7")

## Staff and roles

**People** > **Team** opens Staff and roles.

1. Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then **Invite**.
2. Each row has **Send password link**, **View as (...)** and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).
3. Press **End access** to close their staff portal at once. **Restore** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 780; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff; pins: 1 20.8 59.0, 2 94.4 86.7, 3 83.3 92.6")

## Admin access

**Settings**, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.

1. The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site''s nightly checks sign in with.
2. Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.
3. Change the list only if the business''s Admin address changes.

## Staff scorecards

See how each assistant is doing against the targets.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Scorecard**.
2. By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 350; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 2 21.1 42.9")

## Sales by staff member

See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only **Welcome**, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person''s member tag ("Name - Position") with Copy and the steps; I joined needs **I set my member tag**. The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.

## Work chats only

All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.

## Staff rewards (release 48)

1. **People** > **Team** > **Staff rewards** lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.
2. Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use **Perks** to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.
3. From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month''s top seller gets a free weekend.
4. A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account''s perks are frozen.
5. Free days go on CarmaCars'' and shareholders'' cars first. On a co-host owner''s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).
6. **Add free days** gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Staff rewards**.
