## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking''s all-in price a day) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
1. RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

![](/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program; pins: 1 25.8 22.0, 2 27.8 49.0")


## Lead-time pricing

A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open **Settings**, then **Program settings**: Lead-time pricing is at the top.

1. The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).
2. The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); **Add a tier** adds one, **Remove** takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.
3. **Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer** is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.
4. Press **Save lead-time pricing**. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.

| What it touches | How |
| --- | --- |
| The rental charge | The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, "Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%". Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons |
| When it is worked out | When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. "From $X a day" stays at the base rate |
| When it is locked | On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage |
| Other discounts | The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it |
| Owner revenue and commissions | Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts |
| Staff | Change it on a booking under **More options** on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted |

> Tip: A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: **Vehicles** > the car > **Rates** > Lead-time pricing for this car.
## Vehicle class rules

Open **Settings**, then **Vehicle class rules**. How a new car''s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.

1. The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.
2. Press **Add a rule** or **Change**: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.
3. **Try a car** gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.
4. **Delete** removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.

> Tip: A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.

## Official ServiceOntario forms

The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher''s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. Each form shows "Mapping to check" (a draft is ready) or "Official PDF in use". Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.
2. Choose **Preview with**: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press **Download a filled preview** and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.
3. Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or "Signed here by hand, in ink"), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. **Earlier mappings** lists every save, with who and when; **Load** puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners > Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.
4. Press **Checked: use for owners**. Every owner''s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with **Record an official form signed in ink**. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.
5. A new version from ServiceOntario? Press **Upload the official fillable PDF**: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.

> Good to know: SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company''s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner''s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form''s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.

## Blind Spot rental agreement

We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental''s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars'' rental agreement and Blind Spot''s own. Blind Spot''s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press **Upload Blind Spot''s PDF** and choose Blind Spot''s blank form (2 pages, A4).
2. Press **Download the filled sample**: a made-up booking on the form. **Sample billed to an insurer** also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.
3. On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars'' HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative''s signature instead of Sam''s.
4. Press **Checked: use for bookings**. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.
5. Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.
6. A new version of Blind Spot''s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for **Checked: use for bookings**, and bookings keep the version in use until then.

> Good to know: Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.

The renter''s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking''s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter''s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the "Your signed rental agreement" email. Admin > Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.

## Agreements to sign: investors and staff

Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person''s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).

1. Investor: open **People** > **Investors** and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press **Send the agreement to sign**. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press **Send to sign**.
2. Once the investor signs, the agreement shows **Awaiting countersignature** on the investor''s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press **Countersign**. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.
3. Staff: open **People** > **Team**. Under Staff agreements, press **Send the agreement to sign** beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.
4. A field staff member''s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.
5. They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.
6. Already sent or signed with old terms? Press **Send a new agreement** beside the person: it is filled with the current terms (for staff who live in Canada: Canada, CAD, Interac e-Transfer or direct deposit) and sent to sign the same way. The one waiting is withdrawn; a signed one stays on file, marked superseded, and keeps their portal open until they sign the new one. Someone in Canada still on the old terms (the Philippines, USD, OnlineJobs.ph) shows **Lives in Canada: needs the Canadian terms**, and a To do lists them.
7. Your own PDF instead? **Send a PDF to sign** still works.
8. Sent by mistake? Press **Withdraw** and give the reason.

## The user guides

**Settings** > **Guides**. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.

1. Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.
2. Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press **Show the preview** to see it as people will. Press **Save the draft**; each save is kept in the section''s history.
3. Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press **Add a chapter**. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.
4. Press **Publish version** (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.
5. The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.

## The guides keep up by themselves

After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.

1. Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.
2. The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal''s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.
3. Such a section says **Changed automatically on** and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide''s editor. Not right? Open the section and press **Revert**: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.
4. This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section''s history. There is nothing to review.
5. A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.

> Tip: The card "The guides keep up by themselves" at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.

## Insurers and the other lists

1. Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in **Money** > **Insurers**.
2. To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press **Add**.
3. Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.

## Promo codes: end dates and reminders

**Settings**, **Promo codes**.

- Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.
- A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.
- A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with "This code has expired".
- A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.
- The list shows each code''s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.

## Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage

**Settings** > **Card coverage** is the list renters see at `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage` and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.

1. The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer''s own document, and when it was last checked.
2. Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press **Save**. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.
3. A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer''s own document unticked and the summary''s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer''s guide.
4. Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.

> Tip: A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer''s guide.

## Reviews: review requests and Google

**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press **Change** on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.
3. **Perks**: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. **Change** a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. **Change the response time** sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.
4. Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier''s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner''s payout is worked out on the price before it.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).
5. **Emails and notices to renters**: every Rewards email, each also a notice in the renter''s portal (a text only when they have no email): the welcome, points earned, a new tier, the free day, close to the next tier, points waiting, the 7-day reminder, the free day ending, the monthly statement and the birthday and holiday rewards. Each shows how many went in the last 30 days. **Preview** shows the email with sample values; **Turn off** stops it; **Change** sets the timings or switches them all off. Marketing ones carry an unsubscribe link and never go to someone who unsubscribed.
6. **Birthday and holiday rewards**: a percent off the rental charge by tier for a pickup near the renter''s birthday (7 days either side) or on a holiday weekend: Platinum 10%, Black 20%; Gold is off (0%) until you give it a percent. The bigger one applies, never both, never below the car''s lowest daily price, never on insurer or Owner Bookings. The request or offer keeps it. **Change** a tier for its percents or to switch it off; the holidays are listed with their next weekend: **Turn off**, **Remove** or **Add a holiday** by its date rule.

### Setup checklist
**Settings** shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars'' own accounts. **Add to Apple Wallet** stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker''s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.


Program: **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device''s own phone and messages apps.

## Stuck? help

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Stuck? help**: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. **Where people get stuck**, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.

### API access (Claude and scripts)

Settings > **API access** connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring ("hire Ana as customer service"). **Connect from Claude**: in Claude, Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press **Allow**. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, **Make a key**: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; **Revoke** stops it at once. The **Call log** lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.

### The logo

The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings > **Site settings**, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).

## Deposits stay as holds (release 28)

Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking''s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with **Re-authorize the hold**: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.

**Program settings**: **Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)** is on: Stripe approved it for the account. Every deposit hold (the pay link, the saved card, **Re-authorize the hold**, the reader) asks for a longer authorization, about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise; a card that cannot gets the standard hold by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in **Fees**, editable as every fee.

## Updated terms to accept

**Settings** > **Updated terms**. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with **Requires acceptance** on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.

1. Press **Publish a version**. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).
2. Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and **What changed**: people read this summary first.
3. Paste **The new text**. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site''s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site''s page.
4. Leave **Requires acceptance** on and press **Publish a version**.
5. Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees **We''ve updated our terms** full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.
6. **Accepted** on each version opens who accepted it and when.

> Good to know: It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.

### Card processing fee for a debit deposit
Program settings: **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)** and **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)** (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.

## My profile and name changes (release 34)
Settings > **My profile** has your display name, **Request a name change** for your legal name, your phone number and **Change my password**. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.

## AI auto-replies (release 36)

**Settings** > **Program settings**, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (**Site content**), within Workers AI''s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.

1. A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).
2. When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, **Answer** and the question.
3. Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day''s free AI allowance is used.
4. The card **AI auto-replies: the last answers** shows today''s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.

Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app''s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.

## Address suggestions (release 36)

The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site''s own address database (Statistics Canada''s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.

## Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)

Each card also has: **Network** (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), **Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)** (Yes, No or Unknown), **Vehicle types not covered** (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), **Must decline the rental company''s CDW** and **Must pay the full rental on the card**. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car''s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car''s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in **Program** > **Coverage checks**.

## Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)

- **Program** > **Fuel and charging at the return**: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: **Today** reminds you after 7 days.
- **Airports and delivery** > **Delivery rate and origin**: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company''s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.

## Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)

- Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.
- Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.
- First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.
- Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter''s Rewards page.

## Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)

Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking''s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week''s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner''s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: **Weekly summary email to owners** (on by default).

## Call helper (release 43)

**Settings**, **Call helper**: what staff read inside the caller pop-up while on a call. A change shows on the next call.

1. **Greetings**: one for each kind of caller (a caller we do not know, a renter with a booking, a renter with no booking now, a lead, a car owner, a staff member). Press **Change** and type what to say. `{staff}` becomes the first name of the person on the phone, `{caller}` the caller''s first name, `{booking}` the booking number and `{car}` the car. A greeting that is off, or that needs a name we do not have, falls back to the one for a caller we do not know, which stays on.
2. **Situations**: one button each. **Add a situation** or **Change**: the name on the button, then the steps, one a line (3 to 6 is best, 8 at most). Write a link to a page as `[Bookings](/bookings)`: an Admin gets the Admin page and staff get their own. Words in "quotes" are shown as what to say. **Order** sets the place of the button; switch **On** off to hide one, or **Remove** it.
3. **Quick answers**: the question, the answer, and more search words staff might type.
4. **Numbers from the settings**: never type an amount, a number of days or a percentage. Write its word in braces from this list, for example `{late_grace}` or `{deposit_tiers}`: staff read today''s value from Program settings, Fee defaults and Deposit tiers, and it changes the day the setting does. A word in braces that is not in the list is refused when you save.

Every change is in the audit log with the words before and after.

## Texts and email by message type (release 48)
Program settings, **Texts and email by message type**, lists each message that can go by text with how many texts it sent in the last 30 days. Turn on **Email ready for production** once Amazon SES is out of its sandbox: then only the urgent messages keep their texts (the pickup details and codes, a late return, a failed payment, a declined deposit), and every other message goes by email, by text only when the person has no email address or their email bounced. Press **Change** on a row to send that message by email only, text only, or text and email (the person''s choice). The deposit link, sign-in codes, staff alerts and texts typed by staff always stay texts. While the switch is off nothing changes.

## Deposits by e-Transfer or cash, and tips

1. **Deposit by e-Transfer or cash: a multiple of the deposit** (on) and its multiplier (2): a $300 deposit is $600 by e-Transfer or cash. A debit or prepaid card keeps its own multiplier. An amount set on one booking wins.
2. **Tips** (on): the pay page, the receipt and the after-trip email offer 10, 15 or 20% or an amount; **the salesperson''s share** (5000: half, the rest to the handover).

## The tracker''s price and duplicate leads (release 48)

In **Settings** > **Program settings**:

- The tracker''s price. "GPS tracker product: what a vehicle owner pays for the tracker (0: free)": owners whose cars are listed with us get the tracker free. "GPS tracker product: the number the site says ("free for the first 100 pre-orders")": 100, the number every page shows. "GPS tracker product: how many pre-orders really get the tracker free. Never shown on the site": 250, the count that closes the free offer; no page shows it or how many are left. "GPS tracker product: the pre-order price once the free pre-orders are taken": $90. "GPS tracker product: the regular price after launch": $175, used once "Trackers can be installed" is on. "GPS tracker product: the install price": $150 once per car, paid by everyone, owners included. The tracker pages, the services module, llms.txt and the confirmation email all read these.
- "GPS tracker product: the monthly service price per car by number of cars": the monthly service everyone pays besides the tracker and the install, vehicle owners included. $25 a month per car for 1 or 2 cars, $20 for 3 to 9 and $15 for 10 or more.
- "GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist": the words beside "Join the waitlist" while "Trackers can be installed" is off.
- "Duplicate leads: join a new website form to the person''s open lead" and "Duplicate leads: how many days back the rule looks": whether a new website form joins the person''s open lead by itself, and how many days back it looks.
## Notification preferences (release 48)

1. Everyone chooses their own notifications on their portal: renters and owners under **Account** > **Notifications**, staff, investors and you under **Profile**, partners on their portal link. Each kind has a switch for push, email and text, with quiet hours and instant, a daily summary or a weekly summary.
2. **Settings** > **Notification preferences** shows the kinds people can switch and what each starts as. Press **Change** to set what a kind starts as for everyone who has not chosen.
3. **Always sent** lists the kinds nobody can switch off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, charges and fees, receipts, booking confirmations and changes, pickup and return reminders, safety; for staff, assigned work and onboarding or suspension notices.
4. **People who changed something** opens a person''s choices. A change you make there is logged with your name.
5. **Owner tracker alerts** shows whether they are live (they follow Tracker events in **Cars** > **Fleet tracking** > Tracker event settings, with "Tell the car''s owner" ticked) and the **Places watched**: add the auto shops and shipping ports to watch; a car that stops at one raises an alert for staff and its owner. Impound lots are the **Pound lots** of Fleet tracking.
6. A text that cannot be sent still goes by email, whatever a person chose.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.</p><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-settings-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Settings page</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with <b class="gd-ui">Open site settings</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Program settings: every timing and policy value.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forms: Blind Spot&#39;s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:33%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:84.9%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company&#39;s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">My profile</b>: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole (&quot;Good morning, Abbas and Mahad&quot; on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the greeting name</b>, type it and save.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-program-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Program settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking&#39;s all-in price a day) and <b class="gd-ui">Approve a renter&#39;s extension at once when nothing needs a person</b> (on). A car&#39;s own switch is in Fleet, the car, <b class="gd-ui">Edit details</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Renters extend themselves</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month&#39;s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the defaults</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Change a value and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:22%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.8%;top:49%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-lead-time-pricing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead-time pricing</h2><p class="gd-p">A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: Lead-time pricing is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); <b class="gd-ui">Add a tier</b> adds one, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer</b> is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save lead-time pricing</b>. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What it touches</th><th scope="col">How</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The rental charge</td><td>The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, &quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;. Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons</td></tr><tr><td>When it is worked out</td><td>When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. &quot;From $X a day&quot; stays at the base rate</td></tr><tr><td>When it is locked</td><td>On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage</td></tr><tr><td>Other discounts</td><td>The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it</td></tr><tr><td>Owner revenue and commissions</td><td>Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts</td></tr><tr><td>Staff</td><td>Change it on a booking under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b> on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> &gt; Lead-time pricing for this car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-vehicle-class-rules" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle class rules</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle class rules</b>. How a new car&#39;s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rule</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try a car</b> gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-official-serviceontario-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Official ServiceOntario forms</h2><p class="gd-p">The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher&#39;s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. Each form shows &quot;Mapping to check&quot; (a draft is ready) or &quot;Official PDF in use&quot;. Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Preview with</b>: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download a filled preview</b> and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or &quot;Signed here by hand, in ink&quot;), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b> lists every save, with who and when; <b class="gd-ui">Load</b> puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners &gt; Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for owners</b>. Every owner&#39;s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A new version from ServiceOntario? Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload the official fillable PDF</b>: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company&#39;s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner&#39;s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form&#39;s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-blind-spot-rental-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Blind Spot rental agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental&#39;s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars&#39; rental agreement and Blind Spot&#39;s own. Blind Spot&#39;s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload Blind Spot&#39;s PDF</b> and choose Blind Spot&#39;s blank form (2 pages, A4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled sample</b>: a made-up booking on the form. <b class="gd-ui">Sample billed to an insurer</b> also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars&#39; HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative&#39;s signature instead of Sam&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new version of Blind Spot&#39;s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>, and bookings keep the version in use until then.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking&#39;s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter&#39;s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the &quot;Your signed rental agreement&quot; email. Admin &gt; Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-agreements-to-sign-investors-and-staff" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements to sign: investors and staff</h2><p class="gd-p">Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person&#39;s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Investor: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b>. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once the investor signs, the agreement shows <b class="gd-ui">Awaiting countersignature</b> on the investor&#39;s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">Countersign</b>. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Staff: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b>. Under Staff agreements, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b> beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field staff member&#39;s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Already sent or signed with old terms? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send a new agreement</b> beside the person: it is filled with the current terms (for staff who live in Canada: Canada, CAD, Interac e-Transfer or direct deposit) and sent to sign the same way. The one waiting is withdrawn; a signed one stays on file, marked superseded, and keeps their portal open until they sign the new one. Someone in Canada still on the old terms (the Philippines, USD, OnlineJobs.ph) shows <b class="gd-ui">Lives in Canada: needs the Canadian terms</b>, and a To do lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Your own PDF instead? <b class="gd-ui">Send a PDF to sign</b> still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Sent by mistake? Press <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> and give the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-user-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The user guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b>. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press <b class="gd-ui">Show the preview</b> to see it as people will. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the draft</b>; each save is kept in the section&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a chapter</b>. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish version</b> (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-guides-keep-up-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The guides keep up by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal&#39;s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Such a section says <b class="gd-ui">Changed automatically on</b> and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide&#39;s editor. Not right? Open the section and press <b class="gd-ui">Revert</b>: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section&#39;s history. There is nothing to review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The card &quot;The guides keep up by themselves&quot; at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-insurers-and-the-other-lists" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurers and the other lists</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-promo-codes-end-dates-and-reminders" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Promo codes: end dates and reminders</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Promo codes</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.</li><li>A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.</li><li>A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with &quot;This code has expired&quot;.</li><li>A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.</li><li>The list shows each code&#39;s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> is the list renters see at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer&#39;s own document, and when it was last checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer&#39;s own document unticked and the summary&#39;s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-reviews-review-requests-and-google" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reviews: review requests and Google</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile&#39;s own review link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google Business Profile: press <b class="gd-ui">Connect Google</b> and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A clear match stops that renter&#39;s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and &quot;I already left a review&quot;, Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Pair the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card reader</b>. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Generate pairing code</b>. Type the three words in <b class="gd-ui">Pairing code</b>, name the reader (Front desk) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pair reader</b>. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account&#39;s statement descriptor.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Rewards</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter&#39;s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ways to earn</b>: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend&#39;s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows &quot;Received reward points&quot;), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter&#39;s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tiers</b>: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Perks</b>: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. <b class="gd-ui">Change the response time</b> sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier&#39;s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner&#39;s payout is worked out on the price before it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Google reviews claimed</b> lists every claim; <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> takes the points back with a reason. <b class="gd-ui">A renter&#39;s points</b>: find the renter, then <b class="gd-ui">Add or take off points</b> with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Emails and notices to renters</b>: every Rewards email, each also a notice in the renter&#39;s portal (a text only when they have no email): the welcome, points earned, a new tier, the free day, close to the next tier, points waiting, the 7-day reminder, the free day ending, the monthly statement and the birthday and holiday rewards. Each shows how many went in the last 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> shows the email with sample values; <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops it; <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> sets the timings or switches them all off. Marketing ones carry an unsubscribe link and never go to someone who unsubscribed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Birthday and holiday rewards</b>: a percent off the rental charge by tier for a pickup near the renter&#39;s birthday (7 days either side) or on a holiday weekend: Platinum 10%, Black 20%; Gold is off (0%) until you give it a percent. The bigger one applies, never both, never below the car&#39;s lowest daily price, never on insurer or Owner Bookings. The request or offer keeps it. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a tier for its percents or to switch it off; the holidays are listed with their next weekend: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Add a holiday</b> by its date rule.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Setup checklist</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars&#39; own accounts. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker&#39;s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.</p><p class="gd-p">Program: <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device&#39;s own phone and messages apps.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-stuck-help" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck? help</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Stuck? help</b>: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. <b class="gd-ui">Where people get stuck</b>, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">API access (Claude and scripts)</h3><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">API access</b> connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring (&quot;hire Ana as customer service&quot;). <b class="gd-ui">Connect from Claude</b>: in Claude, Settings &gt; Connectors &gt; Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, <b class="gd-ui">Make a key</b>: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; <b class="gd-ui">Revoke</b> stops it at once. The <b class="gd-ui">Call log</b> lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The logo</h3><p class="gd-p">The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site settings</b>, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-deposits-stay-as-holds-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits stay as holds (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking&#39;s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b>: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)</b> is on: Stripe approved it for the account. Every deposit hold (the pay link, the saved card, <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b>, the reader) asks for a longer authorization, about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise; a card that cannot gets the standard hold by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, editable as every fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-updated-terms-to-accept" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated terms to accept</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Updated terms</b>. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and <b class="gd-ui">What changed</b>: people read this summary first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paste <b class="gd-ui">The new text</b>. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site&#39;s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leave <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b> full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Accepted</b> on each version opens who accepted it and when.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</h3><p class="gd-p">Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)</b> (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-my-profile-and-name-changes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My profile and name changes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My profile</b> has your display name, <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b> for your legal name, your phone number and <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b>. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-ai-auto-replies-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI auto-replies (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (<b class="gd-ui">Site content</b>), within Workers AI&#39;s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day&#39;s free AI allowance is used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The card <b class="gd-ui">AI auto-replies: the last answers</b> shows today&#39;s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app&#39;s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-address-suggestions-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Address suggestions (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site&#39;s own address database (Statistics Canada&#39;s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-the-facts-the-booking-check-uses-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Each card also has: <b class="gd-ui">Network</b> (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), <b class="gd-ui">Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)</b> (Yes, No or Unknown), <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle types not covered</b> (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), <b class="gd-ui">Must decline the rental company&#39;s CDW</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Must pay the full rental on the card</b>. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car&#39;s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car&#39;s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Coverage checks</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-fuel-prices-and-delivery-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Fuel and charging at the return</b>: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> reminds you after 7 days.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports and delivery</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Delivery rate and origin</b>: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company&#39;s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-automatic-answers-and-email-budgets-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.</li><li>Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.</li><li>First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.</li><li>Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter&#39;s Rewards page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-owner-emails-trips-and-the-week-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking&#39;s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week&#39;s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner&#39;s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary email to owners</b> (on by default).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b>: what staff read inside the caller pop-up while on a call. A change shows on the next call.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Greetings</b>: one for each kind of caller (a caller we do not know, a renter with a booking, a renter with no booking now, a lead, a car owner, a staff member). Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> and type what to say. <span class="gd-url">{staff}</span> becomes the first name of the person on the phone, <span class="gd-url">{caller}</span> the caller&#39;s first name, <span class="gd-url">{booking}</span> the booking number and <span class="gd-url">{car}</span> the car. A greeting that is off, or that needs a name we do not have, falls back to the one for a caller we do not know, which stays on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Situations</b>: one button each. <b class="gd-ui">Add a situation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: the name on the button, then the steps, one a line (3 to 6 is best, 8 at most). Write a link to a page as <span class="gd-url">[Bookings](/bookings)</span>: an Admin gets the Admin page and staff get their own. Words in &quot;quotes&quot; are shown as what to say. <b class="gd-ui">Order</b> sets the place of the button; switch <b class="gd-ui">On</b> off to hide one, or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quick answers</b>: the question, the answer, and more search words staff might type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Numbers from the settings</b>: never type an amount, a number of days or a percentage. Write its word in braces from this list, for example <span class="gd-url">{late_grace}</span> or <span class="gd-url">{deposit_tiers}</span>: staff read today&#39;s value from Program settings, Fee defaults and Deposit tiers, and it changes the day the setting does. A word in braces that is not in the list is refused when you save.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Every change is in the audit log with the words before and after.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-texts-and-email-by-message-type-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts and email by message type (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Texts and email by message type</b>, lists each message that can go by text with how many texts it sent in the last 30 days. Turn on <b class="gd-ui">Email ready for production</b> once Amazon SES is out of its sandbox: then only the urgent messages keep their texts (the pickup details and codes, a late return, a failed payment, a declined deposit), and every other message goes by email, by text only when the person has no email address or their email bounced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> on a row to send that message by email only, text only, or text and email (the person&#39;s choice). The deposit link, sign-in codes, staff alerts and texts typed by staff always stay texts. While the switch is off nothing changes.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-deposits-by-e-transfer-or-cash-and-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits by e-Transfer or cash, and tips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Deposit by e-Transfer or cash: a multiple of the deposit</b> (on) and its multiplier (2): a $300 deposit is $600 by e-Transfer or cash. A debit or prepaid card keeps its own multiplier. An amount set on one booking wins.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tips</b> (on): the pay page, the receipt and the after-trip email offer 10, 15 or 20% or an amount; <b class="gd-ui">the salesperson&#39;s share</b> (5000: half, the rest to the handover).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-tracker-s-price-and-duplicate-leads-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The tracker&#39;s price and duplicate leads (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The tracker&#39;s price. &quot;GPS tracker product: what a vehicle owner pays for the tracker (0: free)&quot;: owners whose cars are listed with us get the tracker free. &quot;GPS tracker product: the number the site says (&quot;free for the first 100 pre-orders&quot;)&quot;: 100, the number every page shows. &quot;GPS tracker product: how many pre-orders really get the tracker free. Never shown on the site&quot;: 250, the count that closes the free offer; no page shows it or how many are left. &quot;GPS tracker product: the pre-order price once the free pre-orders are taken&quot;: $90. &quot;GPS tracker product: the regular price after launch&quot;: $175, used once &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is on. &quot;GPS tracker product: the install price&quot;: $150 once per car, paid by everyone, owners included. The tracker pages, the services module, llms.txt and the confirmation email all read these.</li><li>&quot;GPS tracker product: the monthly service price per car by number of cars&quot;: the monthly service everyone pays besides the tracker and the install, vehicle owners included. $25 a month per car for 1 or 2 cars, $20 for 3 to 9 and $15 for 10 or more.</li><li>&quot;GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist&quot;: the words beside &quot;Join the waitlist&quot; while &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is off.</li><li>&quot;Duplicate leads: join a new website form to the person&#39;s open lead&quot; and &quot;Duplicate leads: how many days back the rule looks&quot;: whether a new website form joins the person&#39;s open lead by itself, and how many days back it looks.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-notification-preferences-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notification preferences (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Everyone chooses their own notifications on their portal: renters and owners under <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>, staff, investors and you under <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, partners on their portal link. Each kind has a switch for push, email and text, with quiet hours and instant, a daily summary or a weekly summary.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notification preferences</b> shows the kinds people can switch and what each starts as. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set what a kind starts as for everyone who has not chosen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Always sent</b> lists the kinds nobody can switch off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, charges and fees, receipts, booking confirmations and changes, pickup and return reminders, safety; for staff, assigned work and onboarding or suspension notices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People who changed something</b> opens a person&#39;s choices. A change you make there is logged with your name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner tracker alerts</b> shows whether they are live (they follow Tracker events in <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> &gt; Tracker event settings, with &quot;Tell the car&#39;s owner&quot; ticked) and the <b class="gd-ui">Places watched</b>: add the auto shops and shipping ports to watch; a car that stops at one raises an alert for staff and its owner. Impound lots are the <b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b> of Fleet tracking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A text that cannot be sent still goes by email, whatever a person chose.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

CarmaCars staff in Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales, in the office, remote or in person. Everyone works in one staff portal: its menu shows a group for each function you hold. Read chapter 1, then the chapter for each of your functions. If you also do field work (handovers, returns, moving cars), read the Field Guide too: your jobs are under **Field work** in the same menu.

### What you need

- The invitation email from CarmaCars (the link works for 24 hours)
- A computer for your shift. The portal also works on a phone
- An authenticator app on your phone, if your Admin turns on two-step sign-in

## Once you are hired

You are not working a shift right away. First your training (the academy), then you claim your shifts online in the portal.

1. Say hello in the team chat: the CarmaCars Team WhatsApp group (the link is in your portal once your agreement is signed and the academy is passed).
2. In each WhatsApp group you are in, set your member tag as "Name - Position", for example "Maria - Sales", so everyone knows who you are and what you do.

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours. Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press **Save the new password**.
2. You land in your portal, on **To do**, working as your main function.
3. At the top of the page, fill in your Home address and Postal code and press **Save my home address**. You need it before you add a rental or earn a commission. Change it later under **Profile**, at the top of the menu.
4. Then on **Profile**, **Pay details**: choose how you are paid (bank account, GCash, PayPal, Wise, e-Transfer or through OnlineJobs.ph) and press **Save my pay details**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown; an Admin confirms new details with you.
5. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in` with your Email and Password, then **Sign in**.
6. Link expired? Press **Send me a new link** on the page it opens, or ask an Admin for a password link.
7. Sign in with your phone: on **Profile**, press **Add and verify my phone number** and enter the 6-digit code we text you. Then press **Use my phone number instead** on the sign-in page. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

![](/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg "phone; size: 390 645; pins: 3 95.4 78.4")

> Good to know: Recommended: open your profile and press **Set up two-step sign-in**. Scan the code with your authenticator app, type the 6 digits and press **Continue**. After that every sign-in asks for a code.

## Stuck on a page?

If you work on a page for a few minutes without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the chapter for that page beside it (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Open the Academy lesson** opens the lesson in a new tab. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## Report a bug (release 37)
Something not working? Press **Report a bug** at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (**Blocks my work** alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. **My bug reports** shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won''t fix.

## Work chats only

All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.

## Something to check on your record (release 48)

When something on your record looks wrong, a box opens on any page of the portal and says exactly what, with the box to fix it right there: your staff agreement waiting for your driver''s licence number or home address, a home address outside Ontario while you work in person in Toronto (fix it, or press It''s correct and say why), a licence that expires within 30 days (or has expired), pay details missing, a phone number that is not valid, or your WhatsApp member tag not confirmed. Press **Save** and the box checks again.

1. Your agreement waiting for something you give cannot be put off: once you save it, the agreement is made and appears under Documents to sign at once. The sign page says the same when nothing is ready to sign yet.
2. Anything else you can put off with **Remind me later**: it comes back after a day.

## Your location while you work

The first time, the portal asks you to accept the electronic monitoring policy (you get a copy by email). After that, while you are clocked in or on a job, the portal or the CarmaCars app shares where you are with Admins and Fleet. Off duty nothing is taken. You can turn sharing off in **Profile** > **Location on the live map**, except during an active job.', 'Start here', 'Who this is for and your first sign-in.',
