  '<p class="gd-p">Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.</p><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-which-cars-are-free-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which cars are free (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Calendar</b>: choose the <b class="gd-ui">Pickup</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Return</b> the customer wants and you see every car at once.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car says <b class="gd-ui">Available</b> (green edge) or <b class="gd-ui">Not available</b> (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the <b class="gd-ui">Next free</b> start for the same length of rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Narrow it with <b class="gd-ui">Class</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Seats at least</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Price a day up to</b>, or tick <b class="gd-ui">Available only</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service and Sales: press <b class="gd-ui">Offer these dates</b> on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No customer&#39;s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-the-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The calendar</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by car, plate, booking or name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">With many cars (release 48): filter by <b class="gd-ui">Car status</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Class</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Availability</b> (Fleet and Finance also by owner), and <b class="gd-ui">Group by</b> class, status or availability; press a heading to fold its cars away. The count says how many cars show and how many are free today. <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes the filters off.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A return is a check-out. Under the bars, a trip that ends has two jobs as small chips: <b class="gd-ui">Check-out</b> with its time (once the car is back, the time it actually came back) and <b class="gd-ui">Cleaning</b> (the post-trip cleaning). A tick means done. A booking&#39;s side panel says Pickup (check-in) and Return (check-out).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet and customer service can remove the post-trip cleaning from its side panel (<b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b>) when a car is ready sooner.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/800"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="800"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:60.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:28.5%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car&#39;s page (like CC-7F3A).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Opening a renter&#39;s private details asks for a reason (<b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>). It is kept in the access log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s record has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> for the next 50, and <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. Fleet does not see payments in it.</div></li></ol></div><figure